  "Question": "When constructing the perpendicular bisector of segment $AB$ with a straightedge and compass, arcs are drawn centered at $A$ and $B$. The radius used should be:",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Any length",
    "B": "Less than half the length of $AB$",
    "C": "Greater than half the length of $AB$",
    "D": "Exactly half the length of $AB$"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The radius must be greater than half the length of $AB$ for the two arcs to intersect at two points, thereby determining a line.",
